    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_8c88f6f1b3a46327e3f45734729c1a772ea132b14ee1814d2f1c92ccb2a13c07",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "Nyman–Beurling replaces zero location by completeness: RH is equivalent to density of a family of fractional-part functions in L2(0,1). The accompanying Dirichlet-polynomial formulation makes the same obstruction visible as whether a weighted best-approximation error for 1-A(s)zeta(s) can be driven to zero. This compresses the conjecture into an approximation residual, but the equivalence neither proves density nor makes the infimum tractable.",
